<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hikayat Patani</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hikayat Patani is a Malay chronicle of the sultanate of Pattani on the east coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>, probably compiled in the 17th and 18th centuries. It tells of the founding of the kingdom, the conversion of its ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phaya-tu-nakpa">Phaya Tu Nakpa</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Ismail Shah and the reigns of the four queens, and it describes court customs and ceremonial. It is the main local source for Pattani's early history.</p></div>
